      "text": "Take no thought for your life, Matt. 6:25 (Luke 12:22; 3 Ne. 13:25). Take … no thought for the morrow, Matt. 6:34. Jesus knowing their thoughts said, Matt. 9:4 (Luke 5:22). take no thought how or what ye shall speak, Matt. 10:19 (Mark 13:11; Luke 12:11; D&C 84:84). Jesus knew their thoughts, Matt. 12:25 (Luke 6:8; 11:17). out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, Matt. 15:19 (Mark 7:21). that the thoughts of many hearts may be revealed, Luke 2:35. Jesus, perceiving the thought of their heart, took a child, Luke 9:47. why do thoughts arise in your hearts, Luke 24:38. thought of thine heart may be forgiven thee, Acts 8:22. their thoughts … accusing or else excusing one another, Rom. 2:15. every thought to the obedience of Christ, 2 Cor. 10:5. discerner of the thoughts and intents of the heart, Heb. 4:12.",
